specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/017-deem-search-narrowing-arm/spec.md:3:description: "Measure offline whether one classifier choice that picks a spec track, before ripgrep or the trigger-index lookup searches inside it, beats both zero-call searches at naming the right track. A zero-call default run prints the baseline first. A Jev arm and a Deem arm, Jev first, each run only behind their own switch and checks, and each is kept only if it beats that baseline by a margin fixed here. Built in f7ae1ff44c. The live Deem run printed stop (margin), and the one live Jev run printed keep for jev 0.6.2. Phase 009 was released by the parent D4 amendment of 2026-09-29, not by a keep."
