.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/README.md:79:Five fixtures were captured once, when the lexical lanes were accepted: `latency-report.json`, `semantic-probes.json`, `prompt-set.json`, `recipe-execution.json` and `daemon-off-proof.json`. None has a runtime reader except `semantic-probes.json`, whose Latin paraphrase and exact queries `score-track-narrowing.mjs` reads for a report-only probe line, taking each probe's gold from the current index rather than from the captured paths. Each pins the `manifestHash` of the snapshot it was taken on, and regeneration does not refresh that pin, so a mismatch against the committed manifest is expected and is not a staleness signal. `corpus-manifest.json`, `generation-diagnostics.json` and `phrase-variants.json` are the opposite: every generator run rewrites them, and `/doctor speckit-retrieval` treats a manifest whose hash differs from the committed index as a committed pair that one run did not produce. The manifest's `promptSetHash` stays `null` until a parity consumer pins a prompt set there; the slot is kept so landing that value leaves the manifest hash stable.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/README.md:85:`generate-trigger-index.mjs --check` says whether an index still matches the corpus. It walks and reads the corpus as a build does and compares each document's declared phrases with the phrases the index attributes to it, the same comparison the save path runs for one packet (`lib/freshness.mjs`). It also counts index paths the corpus no longer holds. It writes nothing and exits `0` when nothing differs, `1` when a document is stale, an index path is obsolete or the corpus is untrusted, and `2` on a bad invocation or an unreadable index. A manifest hash that differs while every phrase matches is printed as a note and does not fail the check. It costs one full corpus walk, so it runs as the report-only `advisory-checks.yml` step and by hand, never per lookup.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/README.md:93:| `generate-trigger-index.mjs` | Walks the corpus, reads `trigger_phrases` frontmatter, and publishes one deterministic index plus a manifest and diagnostics; the diagnostics carry a `phraseQuality` bucket that counts every phrase the convention rejects, by class, with the documents that own them. |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/README.md:94:| `lookup-trigger-index.mjs` | Loads the committed index and ranks candidates for one prompt, optionally scoped to a spec folder. The Gate 1 instruction that calls it is authored once, in the root `AGENTS.md` (`CLAUDE.md` is a symlink to it); Pi loads that file from the working directory, while `.codex/AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` carry a pointer block generated from the same line by `runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`, so all five runtimes reach it and `--check` reports a stale copy. |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/README.md:95:| `measure-cold-lookup.mjs` | Spawns one fresh Node process per sample to measure real cold-start lookup latency against a budget. Acceptance-only: nothing runs it on a schedule, and `/doctor speckit-retrieval` offers it as an optional check that writes its report to packet scratch, never to the committed fixture. |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/README.md:96:| `rg-wrapper.mjs` | Builds and runs the structured, path-only and count ripgrep recipes exactly as the convention document specifies, applying the caller-side rank tuple to structured results. |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/README.md:97:| `score-track-narrowing.mjs` | Measures offline whether one classifier choice that picks the spec track beats ripgrep and the trigger-index lookup at naming the right track. The default run makes no model call and writes no file: it prints the test-set counts, both baselines on the same rows, the fixed keep rule and whether a 10-point gain still fits. `--jev` calls its backend only behind that backend's own availability check and needs `--out <dir>` for `calls.jsonl` and `report.json`. It changes no lookup, index or recipe. |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/README.md:98:| `sweep-memory-residue.mjs` | Streams ripgrep JSON-lines matches for retired memory-MCP terms and classifies each hit against an allowlist. Owned by this retrieval package and rerunnable at any time; it was the acceptance check for the memory decommission and stays the residue guard, with the coverage-parity suite keeping its exclusion delta honest. |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/README.md:106:| Index authority | `runtime/data/trigger-index.json` is generated only by `generate-trigger-index.mjs`. No script here hand-edits it. |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/README.md:107:| Scoring parity | `lookup-trigger-index.mjs` and `rg-wrapper.mjs` share normalization and ranking through `lib/normalize.mjs` and `lib/rg-lane.mjs` rather than each re-deriving it. |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/README.md:117:node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs --json
