specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/017-deem-search-narrowing-arm/acceptance-criteria.md:57:In every row, `S` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/score-track-narrowing.mjs` and `STUB` is a directory holding stub `cli-deem` and `jev` binaries that each append one line per invocation to `STUB/calls.log`. In the evidence, `W` is `scratch/w3-build`, and the build is commit `f7ae1ff44c`.
specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/017-deem-search-narrowing-arm/acceptance-criteria.md:61:| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given the real tree, When the script runs without `--deem` or `--jev`, Then it prints per-track counts, both baselines' accuracy, the probe line and the headroom line, calls nothing and writes nothing | `PATH="STUB:$PATH" node S` exits 0 and prints lines starting `baseline lookup:`, `baseline ripgrep:` and either `no headroom` or `planned calls:`. `test ! -s STUB/calls.log && echo no-calls` prints `no-calls`, and `git status --porcelain` is unchanged by the run Observed: `W/runs/zero-call-final` exited 0 in 1,944.1 s and printed `baseline lookup: 17/256 right (0.0664)`, `baseline ripgrep: 68/256 right (0.2656)` and `planned calls: 810 per arm, 256 rows and 14 probes in 3 orders each`. The stub dir held no `calls.log`, and `git status --porcelain` before and after the run is byte-identical (`scratch/w3-build/runs/zero-call-final/stdout.txt:19`, `scratch/w3-build/runs/zero-call-final/stdout.txt:28`, `scratch/w3-build/runs/zero-call-final/exit.txt:1`, build record section 6, and `cmp` of the two status files exit 0 in the closure pass) | Met | - |
specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/017-deem-search-narrowing-arm/acceptance-criteria.md:62:| AC-002 | REQ-002 | Given packets whose descriptions are placeholders or name a track, When the test set is built, Then those rows are dropped and counted, no track keeps more than 20 rows, and no question scores against its own folder | The vitest cases "test set drops a leaking description" and "lookup ignores the question's own folder" pass. On the real tree, the zero-call output prints `kept`, `placeholder`, `leak` and `residual` columns for all 16 tracks with no `kept` value above 20 Observed: the two cases carry the names "drops a description that names a track or a hub and counts it" and "ignores every row inside the question's own folder", and both pass within the file's 33 of 33 (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/score-track-narrowing.vitest.ts:228`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/score-track-narrowing.vitest.ts:293`). The real tree printed 16 `track:` lines with those four columns, the largest `kept` 20, and the total `test set: tracks=16 kept=256 usable=1727 placeholder=67 leak=185 residual=49` (`scratch/w3-build/runs/zero-call-final/stdout.txt:2`, `scratch/w3-build/runs/zero-call-final/stdout.txt:18`) | Met | - |
specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/017-deem-search-narrowing-arm/acceptance-criteria.md:63:| AC-003 | REQ-003 | Given the fresh index, When both baselines score the test set, Then each prints a track accuracy on the same row count and the index `manifestHash` prints | The zero-call output's `baseline lookup:` and `baseline ripgrep:` lines show the same denominator, and an `index manifestHash:` line prints a 64-character hex value equal to `node -p "require('./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/trigger-index.json').manifestHash"` Observed: both lines use the denominator 256, and the run printed `index manifestHash: fdebd12ad1be6133cd344556b5bcdc81ce8736127474d99919f70150342ca67f`, equal to the committed index's `manifestHash` at the time of the runs (`scratch/w3-build/runs/zero-call-final/stdout.txt:1`, `scratch/w3-build/baseline/check.txt:8`, and `git show 64968e9b58:` of the index gives the same value in the closure pass). The session rebuilt the index from committed content after the build commit as `2d101bd6d8`, so a rerun now prints the new hash `7bc9bd5b...`, as `spec.md` section 6 anticipates | Met | - |
specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/017-deem-search-narrowing-arm/acceptance-criteria.md:64:| AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given measured rows in a backend column, When its verdict is computed, Then `keep` needs at least 90 percent of kept rows measured, a gain of at least 10 points, sign-test p below 0.05 and a flip rate of at most 0.10, checked in that order, and anything else prints `stop` with the first failed reason | The vitest cases "verdict keep on stub answers", "verdict stop (margin) on a small gain" and "verdict stop (coverage) with 2 of 10 rows unmeasured" pass and print `verdict deem: keep`, `verdict deem: stop (margin)` and `verdict deem: stop (coverage)`. `PATH="STUB:$PATH" node S` prints `margin: 0.10` and a `keep rule:` line naming all four thresholds before any call line. A saturated fixture prints `no headroom` and the stub log stays empty. The live `--deem` run's `report.json` holds, in the Deem column, the verdict, its reason, K, M, A, B, W, L, F and p, and the verdict equals the stdout line Observed: "prints keep on stub answers that clear all four conditions", "prints stop (margin) on a gain under ten points" and "prints stop (coverage) with 2 of 10 kept rows unmeasured and every measured pick right" pass with those three line prefixes (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/score-track-narrowing.vitest.ts:519`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/score-track-narrowing.vitest.ts:539`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/score-track-narrowing.vitest.ts:561`), and "stops on the sign test and on flips" covers the other two reasons. The zero-call run printed `margin: 0.10` and `keep rule: coverage 10*M >= 9*K, margin 10*(A-B) >= M, sign test p < 0.05, flips 10*F <= 3*M` before the planned-calls line and before any Deem line (`scratch/w3-build/runs/deem-live-1/stdout.txt:22`, `scratch/w3-build/runs/deem-live-1/stdout.txt:23`, `scratch/w3-build/runs/deem-live-1/stdout.txt:28`). "prints no headroom when the baseline is right on more than 90 percent" passes and prints no `planned calls:` line. That case puts no stub on `PATH`, so the empty stub log is derived: the default run spawns no binary (observed with stubs in "default run prints the zero-call report, spawns no model binary and writes no file"), and a switch under `no headroom` prints its skip line before any gate (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/score-track-narrowing.mjs:1968`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/score-track-narrowing.mjs:1990`). The live `report.json` Deem column holds `verdict` `stop`, `reason`, K, M, A, B, W, L, F and p, and its `line` equals the stdout verdict line (`scratch/w3-build/runs/deem-live-1/out/report.json:144`, `scratch/w3-build/runs/deem-live-1/stdout.txt:32`) | Met | - |
specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/017-deem-search-narrowing-arm/acceptance-criteria.md:65:| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given `--deem`, When the Deem check fails, Then the matching skip line prints, the zero-call output is byte-identical and the run exits 0 | With a stub `cli-deem health` reporting backend `stub`, `node S --deem --out <tmp>` prints `deem arm skipped: stub backend` and exits 0, and `diff` of its output minus that line against the default run's output prints nothing. The stub log holds only `health` calls and no `jev` call Observed: "skips a stub backend with the rest of the output byte-identical" passes. It runs `main` with `--deem --out <tmp>` on the fixture corpus, asserts exit 0 and the skip line, asserts the output minus that line equals the default run's output and asserts the stub log equals `['health']` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/score-track-narrowing.vitest.ts:745`). The stub dir holds no `jev` binary, so no `jev` call can appear | Met | - |
specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/017-deem-search-narrowing-arm/acceptance-criteria.md:66:| AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given a default run and each model run, When all finish, Then only the planned paths changed | `git status --porcelain` lists only `score-track-narrowing.mjs`, `score-track-narrowing.vitest.ts`, the retrieval `README.md`, the skill docs of AC-014 and, if inside the repository, the report directory. `git diff --stat -- .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lib .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures .skilled/hooks AGENTS.md` prints nothing Observed: the build's final `git status --porcelain` listed only its ten paths and `W`, which holds the report directories, and the protected-path diff printed nothing (`scratch/w3-build/build-evidence.md:132`, `scratch/w3-build/build-evidence.md:88`). Each run left `git status --porcelain` unchanged. At close, `git show --name-only f7ae1ff44c` lists the ten paths, the Hermes copy of `SKILL.md` that the session regenerated with `sync-skills-hermes.cjs` and 281 files under `W`, and no protected path. The index and fixtures changed only in the session's rebuild from committed content, `2d101bd6d8`, after the build commit | Met | - |
specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/017-deem-search-narrowing-arm/acceptance-criteria.md:67:| AC-007 | REQ-007 | Given a model arm with a passing check, When it asks a question, Then it sends 17 options in three rotations and reduces them to a modal pick | `calls.jsonl` from the live `--deem` run has exactly 3 lines per measured Deem row with order indexes 0, 1 and 2, and `report.json` holds an `optionSetSha256` of 64 hex characters and `options: 17`. In the stub-`jev` vitest run, each row logs 3 `jev choice` calls, each with one `-o` pair per option of that run's option set, the fixture's tracks plus `none` (amended at close, see `goal.md`'s log) Observed: the live `calls.jsonl` holds 810 lines, 270 row ids (256 rows and 14 probes) each with orders 0, 1 and 2, all `measured` (`scratch/w3-build/build-evidence.md:119`, session recount). `report.json` holds `options` 17 (`scratch/w3-build/runs/deem-live-1/out/report.json:129`) and `optionSetSha256` `5562c17c...`, 64 hex characters equal to the stdout hash. In "runs every jev call under one provider and prints keep on stub answers", 6 rows log 18 `choice` lines, each with 3 `-o` pairs, the fixture's 2 tracks plus `none` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/score-track-narrowing.vitest.ts:1178`). Both arms read one option set (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/score-track-narrowing.mjs:1347`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/score-track-narrowing.mjs:1659`), so a real-tree Jev call carries the same 17. That is derived: the live `--jev` run of 2026-09-29 printed `options: 17` with the same `sha256=5562c17c...` and measured 256 of 256 rows, but its `calls.jsonl` records no call arguments (`scratch/w3-build/runs/jev-live-1/stdout.txt:25`) | Met | - |
specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/017-deem-search-narrowing-arm/acceptance-criteria.md:68:| AC-008 | REQ-008 | Given a live model run, When it finishes or stops, Then its notice printed first, every call is recorded and each exit had one handling | The `--deem` run's first arm lines include `nothing leaves the machine` and `planned calls:`. `node -e` over `calls.jsonl` counts 0 Deem lines missing `wallMs`, `exitCode`, `modelId`, `modelCommit` or `sourceCommit` and 0 Jev lines missing `wallMs`, `exitCode`, `jevVersion`, `provider` or `model`. The Jev notice holds `payload:` and `estimated input tokens:` and no `$`. The vitest case for a Deem exit 4 with a changed pair prints `deem arm stopped: model commit changed mid-run`. `node S --deem` or `node S --jev` without `--out` exits 2 with the stub log empty Observed: the live arm printed `deem: nothing leaves the machine; planned calls: 810; ...` after its health line (`scratch/w3-build/runs/deem-live-1/stdout.txt:30`). The session's count over `calls.jsonl` found 0 of 810 lines missing any of the five Deem fields (`scratch/w3-build/build-evidence.md:119`). The live file holds no Jev line, and in the stub Jev run all 19 records carry `wallMs`, `exitCode`, `jevVersion`, `provider` and `model`. The Jev payload line holds `payload:` and `estimated input tokens:` and no `$`. "stops when the commit pair changes after exit 4, or when the backend refuses" passes (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/score-track-narrowing.vitest.ts:911`). After brief 23, the session ran `node S --deem` and `node S --jev` with stub binaries first on `PATH`: each exited 2 in 0 s with empty stdout and the one `needs --out` stderr line, and no stub call was logged (`scratch/w3-build/runs/refusal-check/stderr--deem.txt:1`, `scratch/w3-build/runs/refusal-check/stderr--jev.txt:1`) | Met | - |
specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/017-deem-search-narrowing-arm/acceptance-criteria.md:69:| AC-009 | REQ-009 | Given a verdict, When the report is written, Then it names what the verdict was measured on | `report.json` holds, for the Deem column, `modelCommit` and `sourceCommit` equal to what `cli-deem health` printed at the start, and for a Jev column `jevVersion`, `provider` and `model` equal to the identity and auth test lines. Vitest cases with a stored Deem pair or Jev model that differs print `requalify: model commit changed` or `requalify: model changed` Observed: the live `report.json` Deem column holds `modelCommit` `8cbabbb2c4a7...` and `sourceCommit` `c8a5523c5a7e...`, the pair `scratch/w3-build/runs/deem-live-1/health-before.json` printed, and `requalify.deem` is `null` (`scratch/w3-build/runs/deem-live-1/out/report.json:162`). The live `--jev` run of 2026-09-29 wrote a Jev column holding `jevVersion` `jev 0.6.2`, `provider` `official` and `model` `jev-1.13.0`, equal to its identity line's provider and its `jev: auth test provider=official model=jev-1.13.0` line, and `requalify.jev` is `null` (`scratch/w3-build/runs/jev-live-1/out/report.json:161`, `scratch/w3-build/runs/jev-live-1/stdout.txt:31`). S writes `jevVersion`, `provider` and `model` into the column (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/score-track-narrowing.mjs:1855`). "prints requalify before the verdict when the stored commit pair differs" and "prints requalify when the stored jev model differs" pass (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/score-track-narrowing.vitest.ts:1020`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/score-track-narrowing.vitest.ts:1239`) | Met | - |
specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/017-deem-search-narrowing-arm/acceptance-criteria.md:70:| AC-010 | REQ-010 | Given the 20 Latin paraphrase probes, When any run finishes, Then a probe line prints hits per method and no verdict depends on it | The output holds one `paraphrase probes:` line with the counted gold-less probes and hits for lookup, ripgrep and each model column that ran. The vitest verdict cases give the same verdict with the probe hits changed Observed: the live run printed `paraphrase probes: total=20 gold-less=6 lookup=0/14 ripgrep=8/14 deem=0/14` (`scratch/w3-build/runs/deem-live-1/stdout.txt:33`). The verdict function `summarizeColumn` takes rows, records and baseline picks and no probe input (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/score-track-narrowing.mjs:927`), and the build's verdict cases give `keep` with 0 probes and with 1 probe (`scratch/w3-build/build-evidence.md:143`) | Met | - |
